+### Global custom filters
+
+Use `outlines.prompts.register_filter` to make a Jinja filter available to
+prompts constructed afterwards with `@outlines.prompt`, `Prompt.from_str`, or
+`Prompt.from_file`. Remove it with `unregister_filter`; removing an unknown name
+does nothing.
+
+```python
+from outlines import prompts
+
+prompts.register_filter("surround", lambda value: f"<{value}>")
+prompt = prompts.Prompt.from_str("{{ value | surround }}")
+prompts.unregister_filter("surround")
+
+prompt(value="example")  # '<example>'
+```
+
+Registration is captured when a prompt is constructed, so changing or removing
+a registered filter does not alter existing prompts. Registered filters can
+replace Jinja defaults for future prompts. The Outlines filters `name`,
+`description`, `source`, `signature`, `schema`, and `args` remain protected.
+
 
